    '# Fawri V1 production release readiness\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Purpose\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This document separates **code/runtime readiness** from **real production launch readiness**. A green repository validation does not by itself prove that external production providers, credentials, backups, or cloud permissions exist.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Current integrated code status\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The original validated release-candidate tree `92290d3f97e3ece81525a0b92d668d129e9df5ed` completed 38/38 final integration checks with 0 failures and was merged to `main` through PR #256.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Repository hardening was later merged through PR #281 at:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`5f402a332ef6b9d145aeec326f7800a4e8147ffb`\n' +
      '\n' +
      "That maintenance work intentionally preserved runtime behavior while reorganizing translation authority and extracting cashier-compensation validation from the only executable file above the repository's 1,800-line critical threshold. Because source organization changed, current `main` is no longer byte-for-byte identical to the older release-candidate tree. The final PR #281 head passed the repository audits, focused typechecks/contracts, and all 13 GitHub Actions workflows. PR #282 then advanced documentation only.\n" +
      '\n' +
      'Repository-owned build, typecheck, migration/schema, security, routing, online-order, cashier, merchant/admin/subscription journey, settings, Meta cutover, Knowledge readiness, and related integration gates therefore remain code-ready at the current checkpoint.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This does **not** mean the live production environment is ready. The remaining work is dominated by deployment-time infrastructure, provider credentials/approvals, production backup/restore proof, supported SaaS billing onboarding, and final manual staging/UI validation.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Explicit production release gate\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Production should set:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```text\n' +
      'NODE_ENV=production\n' +
      'FAWRI_DEPLOYMENT_MODE=production\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Production is fail-closed by default: API startup stops before application traffic if required runtime configuration is incomplete. Staging and development must opt out explicitly with `FAWRI_DEPLOYMENT_MODE=staging` or `development`. `FAWRI_PRODUCTION_RELEASE_GATE=required` remains a legacy compatibility marker but production safety no longer depends on it.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Required **Fawri Core runtime** selections include:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- PostgreSQL operational authority: `FAWRI_OPERATIONAL_POSTGRES_AUTHORITY=required`\n' +
      '- a dedicated PostgreSQL runtime role that is not `SUPERUSER`, does not have `BYPASSRLS`, and does not own tenant-protected tables; startup verifies these properties and verifies RLS is enabled on the production tenant-table contract\n' +
      '- PostgreSQL subscription authority: `FAWRI_SUBSCRIPTION_POSTGRES_AUTHORITY=required`\n' +
      '- PostgreSQL merchant Auth sessions: `FAWRI_AUTH_POSTGRES_SESSION_AUTHORITY=required`\n' +
      '- strong `FAWRI_AUTH_SECURITY_SECRET`\n' +
      '- safe HTTPS `FAWRI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`\n' +
      '- `FAWRI_SERVICE_VERSION`\n' +
      '- strong `FAWRI_OBSERVABILITY_BEARER_TOKEN`\n' +
      '- core background workers enabled\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Meta, AI/Knowledge providers, AWS KMS for Meta credentials, SaaS billing, production backup/restore, and durable support-image storage are **external launch integrations/blockers**, not prerequisites for starting the provider-neutral Fawri Core. Until Meta is intentionally activated, keep `FAWRI_META_CUTOVER_READY=0`, `FAWRI_META_REPLY_TRANSPORT=disabled`, and `FAWRI_META_CREDENTIAL_PROVIDER=disabled`. When an external integration is activated, its own fail-closed readiness contract applies.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The release gate reports only safe error codes. Secret values must never be returned in readiness responses or startup logs.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'A non-secret deployment template is provided at `.env.production.example`. It is documentation only: real values must be populated through the deployment secret store/workload identity and must never be committed.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Meta production activation\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Meta OAuth is fail-closed by default. `/api/meta/login` and `/api/meta/callback` become reachable only when the PostgreSQL/KMS/live-send activation contract is explicitly configured. The repository contains no Replit callback fallback.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Production requirements outside source control remain:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- Meta application approved/configured for the intended production use;\n' +
      '- real `META_APP_ID`, `META_APP_SECRET`, `META_CONFIG_ID`, `META_VERIFY_TOKEN`;\n' +
      '- production HTTPS callback registered with Meta and exactly matching `META_REDIRECT_URI`;\n' +
      '- webhook subscription/configuration for the production app/pages;\n' +
      '- AWS workload identity/IAM and KMS key policy permitting the documented decrypt operation;\n' +
      '- wrapped production DEK manifest generated and stored through the deployment secret system.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Do not validate these by committing credentials or sending test traffic from CI.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Knowledge production activation\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The OpenAI-backed Knowledge providers are optional external integrations and are not required for provider-neutral Fawri Core startup. When AI/Knowledge is intentionally activated, configure the selected `FAWRI_KNOWLEDGE_*_PROVIDER` values and provide `OPENAI_API_KEY` through the deployment secret store. Repository tests use non-real/injected values only.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## SaaS subscription billing blocker\n' +
      '\n' +
      "Fawri's SaaS billing authority is server-authoritative, but the currently implemented checkout providers are not a production payment path:\n" +
      '\n' +
      '- `superqi_sandbox` is test-only and production-forbidden;\n' +
      '- `fastpay` remains `merchant_setup_required` until Fawri receives the official merchant onboarding/credentials and supported integration contract.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Therefore **automated production SaaS subscription purchase/renewal is an external launch blocker**. Do not invent provider endpoints, signatures, settlement behavior, or success callbacks.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Merchant-customer payments are a separate domain. Fawri does not custody merchant-customer funds; manual merchant confirmation is supported and future provider evidence is provider-neutral.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Production backup/restore blocker\n' +
      '\n' +
      "The repository's current backup/restore scripts and runbook intentionally support disposable validation targets only. They are not production backup infrastructure.\n" +
      '\n' +
      'Before launch, the owner/infrastructure environment must provide and prove:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- the actual production PostgreSQL backup mechanism;\n' +
      '- backup encryption/access controls and retention policy;\n' +
      '- the actual production object/media backup mechanism if object storage is used;\n' +
      '- restore to an isolated recovery target;\n' +
      '- a documented restore drill with integrity verification;\n' +
      '- RPO/RTO ownership and alerting.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'A disposable local drill is useful regression evidence but does not satisfy this production requirement.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Durable support-image storage blocker\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The runtime release gate also reports:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '`SUPPORT_IMAGE_DURABLE_STORAGE_EXTERNAL_PROOF_REQUIRED`\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Support images are currently stored through a filesystem-backed storage path. Production must prove that the selected hosting environment provides durable persistent storage with restart/redeploy survival, private access, retention/deletion behavior, multi-instance consistency where applicable, and backup/restore coverage. If the production host is ephemeral, a durable storage-provider implementation must be completed before launch.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Release sequence\n' +
      '\n' +
      '1. Merge only code that passes repository typecheck/build, migrations, PostgreSQL runtime integration, Meta live-transport regressions, and release-gate tests.\n' +
      '2. Prepare production PostgreSQL and apply the committed migration chain through the latest version using a migration-owner role. Provision a separate restricted runtime role with the required grants; the runtime role must not be superuser, must not have BYPASSRLS, and must not own tenant-protected tables.\n' +
      '3. Configure production secrets through the deployment secret store, never source control.\n' +
      '4. Configure AWS KMS/IAM and validate bootstrap/readiness from the production workload.\n' +
      '5. Configure the Meta production application/callback/webhook and verify OAuth against a controlled test merchant/page.\n' +
      '6. Configure OpenAI credentials and confirm Knowledge readiness.\n' +
      '7. Establish and prove production backup/restore.\n' +
      '8. Prove durable support-image storage for the selected production hosting model.\n' +
      '9. Complete a production SaaS billing-provider integration only from official provider documentation/credentials.\n' +
      '10. Set `FAWRI_DEPLOYMENT_MODE=production` and require startup plus `/ops/readiness` to be ready before routing traffic.\n' +
      '11. Run controlled end-to-end smoke tests and observe queues/DLQ/alerts before general launch.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## Current readiness interpretation\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Repository validation establishes **Fawri Core production-runtime code readiness** for the integrated tree. This document intentionally avoids pinning that statement to an obsolete historical `main` SHA; the current branch/commit and required CI evidence are the release source of truth.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'It must not claim **production launch readiness** while any of the following remain unresolved:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- `SAAS_BILLING_PRODUCTION_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE`\n' +
      '- `PRODUCTION_BACKUP_RESTORE_EXTERNAL_PROOF_REQUIRED`\n' +
      '- `SUPPORT_IMAGE_DURABLE_STORAGE_EXTERNAL_PROOF_REQUIRED`\n' +
      '- production PostgreSQL deployment/migration proof and restricted runtime-role grants,\n' +
      '- production AWS KMS/IAM/wrapped-DEK readiness,\n' +
      '- production Meta application/OAuth/webhook/live-send readiness,\n' +
      '- production OpenAI credential/readiness,\n' +
      '- final full-stack staging and manual UI/UX validation,\n' +
      '- production release-gate and controlled smoke-test evidence.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Actual credentials, cloud permissions, provider approvals, production backups, and live-provider behavior are deployment-time evidence and must never be represented by repository test fixtures.\n'
    
  code: 'ERR_ASSERTION'
